# package.accept_keywords for the amdkdehard live image.
#
# Verbatim copy of this host's /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/
# {moje,systemowe}.keywords, taken 2026-08-04.
#
# Why the image needs it at all: PROF_LIVE_PKGS in profiles/amdkdehard.conf
# is this host's world(5), and 45 of those atoms — awscli-bin, keepassxc,
# suricata, lynis, hashcat, zen-sources, every *-bin browser, all twelve
# ::pwr overlay atoms — have no stable amd64 keyword. A keyword mask is a
# resolver error, so emerge aborts the whole run on the first one rather than
# skipping it; --keep-going cannot help. The image's portage profile leaves
# ACCEPT_KEYWORDS at stable amd64, which is the right default for a hardened
# image, so the exceptions have to be named.
#
# Copied whole rather than reduced to those 45 on purpose: this is the exact
# list that made the same package set build on this host, dependencies
# included, and a dependency masked one level down aborts the run just as
# hard as a top-level atom. Entries naming packages the image does not carry
# are inert.
#
# The alternative, ACCEPT_KEYWORDS="~amd64" image-wide, is one line but puts
# the entire userland on testing — the opposite of what this profile is for.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   cat /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/{moje,systemowe}.keywords

app-arch/xz-utils **
app-misc/openrgb **
app-misc/colibri **
dev-libs/xrt-xdna **
dev-python/bitsandbytes **
